1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,620
I started skydiving very early, at 17, and began BASE jumping at 20.

2
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:14,260
At that age, as a young man, you generally have very little fear.

3
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:20,720
Even when I was skydiving, people were always talking about being careful and about accidents.

4
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:24,120
And I always thought, "Yeah, yeah, that won't happen to me."

5
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:31,120
Now I'm wiser. As you get older, you naturally become more cautious.

6
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:37,680
I've also been in the sport for quite a while now, and you witness accidents or see them yourself.

7
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:44,260
That teaches you a lot. Accidents can happen to anyone, even the very best.

8
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:47,580
That's something you learn over time, and I've definitely become much more cautious.

9
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:51,760
I'd say I was never reckless, not even in the beginning.

10
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:55,140
But I've definitely become more cautious over the years.